#title: span

[Span<T>|
Provides a type-safe and memory-safe
representation of a contiguous region
of arbitrary memory.|
Span(ref T reference)
Span(T\[\]? array)
Span(void* pointer, int length)
Span(T\[\]? array, int start, int length)|
static Span<T> Empty { get }
bool IsEmpty { get }
ref T this\[int index\] { get }
int Length { get }|
void Clear()
void CopyTo(Span<T> destination)
void Fill(T value)
Span<T>.Enumerator GetEnumerator()
ref T GetPinnableReference()
Span<T> Slice(int start)
Span<T> Slice(int start, int length)
T\[\] ToArray()
bool TryCopyTo(Span<T> destination)|
static bool operator ==(Span<T> left, Span<T> right)
static bool operator !=(Span<T> left, Span<T> right)
static implicit operator Span<T>(ArraySegment<T> segment)
static implicit operator ReadOnlySpan<T>(Span<T> span)
static implicit operator Span<T>(T\[\]? array);
]

[ReadOnlySpan<T>|
Provides a type-safe and memory-safe 
read-only representation of a contiguous
region of arbitrary memory.|
ReadOnlySpan(ref readonly T reference)
ReadOnlySpan(T\[\]? array)
ReadOnlySpan(void* pointer, int length)
ReadOnlySpan(T\[\]? array, int start, int length)|
static ReadOnlySpan<T> Empty { get }
bool IsEmpty { get }
ref readonly T this\[int index\] { get }
int Length { get } |
ReadOnlySpan<T> CastUp<TDerived>(ReadOnlySpan<TDerived> items)
void CopyTo(Span<T> destination)
ReadOnlySpan<T>.Enumerator GetEnumerator()
ref readonly T GetPinnableReference()
ReadOnlySpan<T> Slice(int start)
ReadOnlySpan<T> Slice(int start, int length)
T\[\] ToArray()
bool TryCopyTo(Span<T> destination)|
static bool operator ==(ReadOnlySpan<T> left, ReadOnlySpan<T> right)
static bool operator !=(ReadOnlySpan<T> left, ReadOnlySpan<T> right);
static implicit operator ReadOnlySpan<T>(ArraySegment<T> segment);
static implicit operator ReadOnlySpan<T>(T\[\]? array);
]